So! Finally a wizard ascension. Previous best try got killed by &, &
and & (Orcus, Yeenoghu and Demogorgon).

Well, this gnomish Wizard did quite well, started with a Magic Marker,
ususally a sign I'll die an early YASD, but not this time. Found a
silver dagger relativly early and used that along with some throwing
daggers as my main non- magical weapons.

Me and my cat Mr.Jones were doing all right, sometime later a dog
joined us and a polymorph trap in Gehennom got me a flesh golem named
Mr.Jones and an elven King, very nice. After donating some in Mine
Town, the priest there had an accident, very sad.

Found an altar on Dlvl 14, moved stash from Mine Town there and
started sacrificing. Soon got spellbooks and when I moved the
sacrificing party to Dlvl 21, got Magicbane and the castle tune.
Cleared the Castle, finally got XL 14 and went to do the Quest.
Nothing much to report there. Wished for a SDSM, since none of the
Castle dragons were silver and between the Eye of the Aethiopica and
not being able to wear a shield of reflection...
Magicbane got enchanted to +3, I know there's some way to get that to
+2 again, but I didn't bother, in the end another accidental
enchanting got it to +4. As my secondary weapon I had a blessed +6
silver dagger, used whenever there was little chance of catching
curses and the additional silver damage was appropriatly used.

Spend sometime sacrificing and #praying on the Dlvl 21 altar, received
lots of spellbooks, amongst those polymorph and magic missile. Got
crowned for a FoD spellbook. Did some quite successful nurse dancing.

Very much later finally got some level ups to XL 18, even uncursed a
!oGL which I had planned for the Sanctum, but dig at 66% fail was too
much bother and uncontrolled levitation wasn't my thing neither, so I
needed skill slots.

While moving my stash from Dlvl 21 to the VotD temple, nethack crashed
due to my harddisk being full so it couldn't successfully do the level
change... Thankfully all I lost was the way from the stairs to the
Dlvl 21 altar stash and back to the downstairs, so I could use my
savegame backup without too much of a bad conscience, since the second
time was much like the first time there wasn't anything bad happening
the first time that I skipped the second time and nothing good that
happened the second time as opposed to before the crash...

Don't know what I'd've done if it had been in a different situation,
like blowing up my BoH and then having to restore from a crash or
something, I mean I'd have been morally obliged to blow up the bag
again... I think I'd just've started a new game then...

Mr Jones the Flesh Golem didn't survive a large graveyard on Dlvl 18,
the Elf King got killed sometime later.

Well, polymorph was at 50% got some more spellbooks, amongst others
light (very nice for jumping spell), magic mapping and charm monster.

Enchanted stuff up, wished for a cornuthaum, very nicemost groovy
wizard hat, much more stylish than a HoB anyway. Also wished for two
magic markers and a replacement CoMR, since I got confused and thought
armor could be enchanted safely from +4. Oh yeah, one of those wishes
from a b !oHealing, which were smoky.

Had a nice stack of 24 +6 blessed elven daggers, very nice to conserve
energy :).

Had the invocation items at the VS around turn 60.000. Did some
alchemy and some final enchanting. Put together my AK, including some
spellbooks of not yet expired spells that were too close to being
forgotten, WoD and WoT some of Cold. Well, the usual stuff.

Went to wake up Rodney, who immediatly double troubled, but other than
having to FoD two of them, no problem. All in all Rodney showed up 5
times, was FoD'd everytime.

Did the run. The Sanctum was a bit crowded, but not for long. FoD
rules :) Got the Amulet, did the run up, wasn't thrown back too much.
Showed Neferet the Green the AoY, who was very proud of me, well me
too :).

Found out just how much Magicbane is cool, never had anything cursed
and it did decent damage. Together with magic missile, FoD and the +6
silver dagger, the only problem I had was, as usual, on Air, where the
Air Elementals were being_very_ mean. Especially in the clouds, not
nice that, but survivable.

Earth had been easy, two zaps of the WoD and I was at the portal,
Rodney having been FoD'd a final time.

Fire also no problem, evaded some monsters and went through the
portal.

Water took a bit longer, until I floated to the correct bubble. Didn't
use levitation this time, since i figured that the portal was going to
be in one of the air bubbles anyway, and I didn't have any problems
there.

Oh yeah, found all four portals by confused ?oGD.

Astral Plane had Famine left, Death middle and Pestilence right. The
AoY did lots of power draining and by the time I had found out that
Famine was guarding the wrong altar and had made my way past
Pestilence to the right, I was down to 30 Pow or something. So I cast
charm monster and rested behind my newly acquired insect pets. Then
made my way to the temple, helped by Eva the Valkyrie's blasts of a
WoDeath. This temple was of Toth, so I offered the AoY and that's
that.

